WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.592 --> 00:00:02.350
(jaunty music)
- Welcome royal punters

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:04.360
to "The Crown" Pub, grab a pint,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.180
and get ready to play the
official "Crown" Pub Quiz.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.290
Corgi related player names
are optional but welcomed.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:11.230
You'll need to fetch a pen and paper

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.790
and grab some friends.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.400
Answers will be given after each round.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.360
So make sure you swap your sheets.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.010
Any cheating will be frowned upon.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:22.130
This quiz consists of
three rounds, trivia,

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.750
true or false, and guess who?

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.810
Ready?

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.290
Hit pause if you still need to find a pen.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.370
Round one is all about episode one,

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.520
and it's about to start.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.362
So we'll hand you over to our barman Tom.

00:00:33.362 --> 00:00:34.610
(bell dinging)

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.600
- In what year did the first episode

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.422
of season three take place?

00:00:39.422 --> 00:00:42.089
(clock ticking)

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.690
What is the value of the stamp

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.663
with Olivia Colman's portrait on it?

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.643
What was Harold Wilson's KGB code name?

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.860
What command does Philip
give Anthony Blunt

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.193
when he wants to give
the Queen a quick kiss?

00:01:40.205 --> 00:01:43.538
What is the name of Margaret's new maid?

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.200
Which coin does Elizabeth remember

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.853
first seeing her father on?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.180
What song does Margaret sing at the piano

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.253
while Tony is developing photos?

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.620
What is the graffiti slogan on the photo

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.960
that Tony is developing
while Margaret's singing

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:30.873
in the other room?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.653
Which university did
Michael Straight attend?

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.173
- [Announcer] Big thanks to Tom

00:02:57.173 --> 00:02:59.100
for that pint of trivia.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.610
Now onto the bonus round

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.550
hosted by two very special punters.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.982
You can score two points for
every answer you get correct.

00:03:06.982 --> 00:03:08.130
(bell dinging)
Here we go.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.987
- Who is the writer of "The Crown?"

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.350
- How did Princess Margaret

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.403
supposedly like to start her day?

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.933
- What is Queen Elizabeth's
favorite cocktail?

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.660
- [Announcer] Thanks to Josh and Erin

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.450
who just happened to be in
the pub at the right time.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.200
Truly, what are the chances?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.000
Now it's time to swap your
sheets and mark your answers.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.670
Number one, 1964.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.800
Number two, sixpence.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.890
Number three, olding.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.100
Number four "eyes left."

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.020
Number five, violet.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.020
Number six, shilling.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.400
Number seven, just one of those things.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.930
Number eight, eat the rich!

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.060
Number nine, Cambridge.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.670
And here are the bonus round answers.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.820
Remember it's two points for each.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.110
Number 10, Peter Morgan.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.400
Number 11, you could have
having breakfast in bed,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.860
listening to the radio,
or reading the papers.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.890
Because we're giving you
two points for any of those.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.210
Number 12, Dubonnet and gin.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:51.310
OK, snatch back your answer
sheet and see how you did.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.510
If you need an extra
minute, just hit pause.

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:57.920
Whenever you're ready, our
landlady and queen of drag

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.605
Jodie Harsh will take you
through the true or false round.

00:05:01.605 --> 00:05:02.759
(bell dinging)

00:05:02.759 --> 00:05:05.050
- True or false, costume designers

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.010
on "The Crown" had to
stitch the word sample

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:11.620
into every single outfit
that Claire Foy wore

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.470
to comply with counterfeiting laws

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.224
with regards to Her Majesty's likeness?

00:05:16.224 --> 00:05:19.307
(brassy dance music)

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.760
True or false, set
designers on "The Crown"

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.720
had to especially custom design

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.450
the door of 10 Downing
Street for John Lithgow

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:37.400
because he's a foot taller than
Churchill was in real life.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.480
True or false, Prince
Philip was such a big fan

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.620
of Mary Berry on "The
Great British Bake Off"

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.317
that he refuses to watch
the new Channel 4 series.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.730
True or false, according
to an old golfing buddy

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.700
who caught a glimpse in the shower,

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.033
the Duke of Windsor has no pubic hair.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.930
True or false, the
corgis on set are treated

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.100
even more lavishly than the
Queen's are, in real life.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.840
They're treated to a three
course meal of rabbit,

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.173
duck, and grouse twice a day.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:55.810
True or false, Helena Bonham
Carter is 59th in line

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.873
to the throne through her
uncle, Lord Bonham Carter.

00:07:11.258 --> 00:07:14.330
True or false, because
fabric rationing was in place

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.340
when the Queen and Philip got engaged,

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:18.530
the Queen had to save up her ration cards

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.783
to get a wedding dress.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.520
True or false, as well as
photographing the actual Queen,

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.550
photographer Tony Armstrong
Jones also shot the cover art

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:41.363
for "Queen's Greatest Hits" album.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.330
- [Announcer] Thanks Jodie,
that round was truly harsh.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:55.300
It's that time again.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.950
Swap your sheets and get marking.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:05.530
Here are your answers, number one, false.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.104
Number two, true.

00:08:07.104 --> 00:08:08.940
Number three, false.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.400
Number four, true.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:11.752
Number five, false.

00:08:11.752 --> 00:08:13.520
Number six, false.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:14.760
Number seven, true.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.023
And number eight, true.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.210
Answer sheets at the ready!

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.010
It's time for round three.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.650
If you need a bit more
time, hit pause now.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:25.920
When you're ready, Jodie's
back with the final round.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.387
Get ready to guess who.

00:08:28.469 --> 00:08:29.370
(bell dinging)

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:31.340
- Which royal is casually known

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:34.423
to her university friends as Sesh Gremlin?

00:08:37.404 --> 00:08:40.487
(upbeat disco music)

00:08:46.912 --> 00:08:50.320
Which royal created the
children's storybook character

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.893
Budgie the Little Helicopter?

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:06.470
Which royal had a real sweet tooth,

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.670
allegedly developing a daily habit

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:10.793
for Choco Leibniz biscuits?

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:25.310
Which royal allegedly had a
short-lived email relationship

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:26.683
with Britney Spears?

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:42.800
Which royal supposedly
hates horse racing so much

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.400
that they have a secret room at Ascot

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.700
where they can sneak off
and watch TV instead?

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.510
Which royal is said to
have once dressed up

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:04.020
in fighter pilot disguise to
enjoy an anonymous night out

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:06.570
down at Royal Vauxhall
Tavern with Freddie Mercury?

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.890
Which royal has a very simple rider

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:24.403
when making public appearances,
a can of full-fat Coke?

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:39.450
Which royal played tambourine

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.397
on the Gary Barlow track, "Sing?"

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:56.150
Which Royal is a keen reggae enthusiast

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.493
and a huge fan of Rihanna?

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.450
- [Announcer] OK, that's
the end of our quiz.

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.060
But before you go, swap
sheets, and get ready to mark.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.810
'Cause here come the final answers.

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.520
Number one, Princess Eugenie.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:22.800
Number two, Fergie.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.500
Number three, Princess Margaret.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:25.830
Number four, Prince William.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.570
Number five, Prince Philip.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:29.332
Number six, Lady Diana.

00:11:29.332 --> 00:11:31.540
Number seven, Princess Anne.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:32.810
Number eight, Prince Harry.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:34.773
And number nine, Prince Charles.

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:39.793
Time to tot up your total marks out of 32.

00:11:45.517 --> 00:11:47.750
Right, that's last orders.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.460
Over to Jodie to close up.

00:11:49.460 --> 00:11:51.460
- Well I hope you enjoyed the quiz.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.090
Thanks for stopping by "The Crown."

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:56.993
And now it's time for
you to get outta my pub!

